> Hello,
> 
> How can I remove a BSD Disk Label to a 'normal' Linux partition ???

If you want to remove the disklabel and create a new partition table
you can wipe out the old one with 

dd if=/dev/zero of=/dev/your/disk count=1

Then run fdisk and create your partitions. This is likely to destroy
data on at least the first partition, so use carefully.

If you are trying to convert a disklabel into a dos partition table it
can't be done.

