> > I'm not sure why the kernel would be unable to reference disks because
> > of being invoked from SRM instead of AlphaBIOS, when if the kernel is
> > running, then you've got neither SRM nor AlphaBIOS running...
>
> The issue is that in general AlphaBIOS systems use a DOS style
partitioning
> scheme (in particular, they must have a FAT partition at the start of the
disk)
> whereas SRM booted systems have a different partitioning scheme and the
boot
> loader is written at the start of the disk.
>
> I don't see how you can build a disk that is booted from one and then is
> sucessfully booted from the other. Of course, you can boot from some other
> device (even a floppy) and probably get that to work, but I was assuming
that
> the original question was "can I change from AlphaBIOS to SRM and boot
> from the same disk without making changes"
