Since I had an opportunity to try new Tekram Ultra 2 Wide SCSI host
adapter on AXPpci, I noticed that it does not perform much better than
the on-board SCSI interface.  On-board 53c810 interface transfers
about 4 to 5 MB per second from IBM Ultrastar 18ES (9 GB/7200 RPM)
narrow SCSI harddisk.  This new 53c895 reads up to 6 MB per second
from new IBM Ultrastar 36LP (18 GB/7200) harddisk.

On new wintel computer I had to build (for someone else, fortunately),
it is possible to read about 29 MB per second from the same 36LP
harddisk with that 53c895.

The point is, I was planning to get new harddisk and controller for
AXPpci.  If the performance is not better than this, I should think
again (about saving money for more recent Alpha, PowerPC or SPARC
computer instead).

Is the PCI bus on AXPpci that slow or does my system have some other
problem?  Alpha is running Linux 2.2.19, optimized for the system and
built to only contain drivers for devices I have on it.  The support
for newer 53c8xx SCSI adapters was added before testing.

