I've exactly the same system running (AS1000 4/266) with RedHat 7.1. You
don't need any extra tricks, it runs out-of-the-box
Do the following (in SRM):
boot dka400 -fl root=/dev/scd0
Then it stops in aboot. You can choose predefined configs here. (l lists)
choose 3 for text. Or an other for grafical, but i didn't test those...

Installing on a 1 Gb Hdd IS possible, but a 2 or 4Gb Hdd is advisable

-paul-




