Those are the two ide controllers,  pqa0 = dqa0 master, dqa1 slave
pqb0=dqb0 master, dqb1 slave..
the only problem in on the 433, 500 etc those ide controller are only good
for running a cd-rom drive. They never worked correctly to allow VMS or Unix
to use them for hard drives. There has been "some" success with Linux, but
no DMA.

Yes you can create boot floppies on a windows system, put your RH cd into
your Usoft system and look in the images directory.. you should find a dos
utility caller "rawrite" which will copy a "floppy image file (.img)  from
the CD to a floppy, using windows.  The floppy boot images should be around
there also.

jj
