Download the SRM image here:

ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/v6.1/alphapc164lx/

Download the lx164srm.rom file and put it on a floppy

Then go to AlphaBios update with the floppy installed

This will then load the SRm console onto the FLASH on the chip on PC164LX
board

Power cycle (switch it off for at least 5 seconds)

Bring it back up and then it should be at the SRM console

This looks like this:

>>>

Basic instructions

>>>sh dev

THis shows devices such as cdrom disk etc and gives a name ot each device
e.g. disk is say dkc0, cd is dka0 ethernet ewa0

Make sure you have a scsi controller that is either a Qlogic QLA1020/QLA1040
or a NCR53C875 based card
Adaptec WILL Not work to boot from

You will need to set the variables in the SRM before booting
For linux type the following:

>>>set os_type Unix
>>>set boot_osflags 0


To boot

>>> b dxxx (device name)


This should do it !




