I dug around for some more info on this problem and discovered that the
problem with this was the RPMs provided from Red Hat.  I read on another
newsgroup that upgrading to the most current RPM for wu-ftpd did NOT fix the
problem.  Compiling wu-ftpd from the source, however, was said to fix this
issue, and therefore that is what I did to get us working.  This can be
obtained from http://www.wu-ftpd.org/ .  There is also a problem with the
ftp RPM (ftp-0.17-6) provided by Red Hat.  I did not try compiling ftp from
the source but it has been reported that it also works fine by compiling
it.  A workaround would be to use the ncftp client instead, which works fine
from Red Hat.

Both the wu-ftpd and ftp RPMs supplied by Red Hat are faulty, and are
specific to the Alpha versions only.  Intel versions work fine with no
problems.

Hope this will help somebody else out....

--
Chris

